ifSeedT -- SEQ 422 R0 (2026-10-26): docket item (a), a value seeded in an if's then-arm and read after its endif, in a
compiled action (tpTestResult's shape: `if c; *h = 1;` then `if *h == 1; ...`). Each holder is minted at top level, so no
dereference is handed over to run time.

IS-1 isAfter -- today NOT JITTABLE, compile -5 (the post-join read reuses the arm's load, which does not dominate it);
interpreted, so its values = the twin. Intended: compiled, built 1, values = the twin.
IS-C1 isInside, the read INSIDE the arm -- compiles, and reads isIn 0 against the twin's 1.
IS-C2 isBoth, if / else seeding both arms -- today -5 as well.
IS-C3 isLoop, a seed in a while body read after the loop -- today -5 as well.
IS-S isStale, a read BEFORE the if (its load dominates the post-join read) -- compiles, verifies, and runs WRONG: 0 0 0
against the twin's 1 1 1.
SN-1 / SN-2 the star alone: `*h = 1` writes nothing (the star's node is consumed as the assignment's RIGHT side), and a
star in a condition leaks its node into the arm's `snA = snA + 1`. Both compile, both wrong, silent.
